  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water challenges at the Game Changer Challenge South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">During the UN2023 Gamechanger Challenge (08/2022-03/2023), youth from all over the world have submitted their proposals to contribute to a more water-secure world. During the 2023 Ocean Race stopover in Cape Town (09/02/2023-28/02/2023), the aim is to connect South African participants of the UN2023 Gamechanger Challenge (youth, including women) and the South African network of the World Urban Forum (WUF) to the local private water sector, local communities, vocational education groups, universities and local youth networks for water, to further develop their ideas in actual implementable projects for local private sector, entrepreneurs and government in South Africa. This supports private sector development in the South African water sector, addresses youth unemployment and accelerates actions towards a more water-secure world.</narrative>
  </description>
